---
name: conversation-image-scenes
description: Author an image for the current conversation while preserving permanent appearance and the recorded day.
---

For a conversation image, author the scene using the structured scene builder with all 8 core parameters:
subjects, setting, clothing, action, pose, expression, camera, and lighting (plus optional details).
Imagined scenes and image-only outfits do not update your presence or wardrobe. Recorded context
is available when useful, but does not constrain a clearly imagined picture.
Do not invent real facts about the human.

Read context when needed:
`{{IMAGE_COMMAND}} context`

Preview without rendering:
`{{IMAGE_COMMAND}} preview --require-structured --camera "..." --subjects "..." --expression "..." --pose "..." --action "..." --clothing "..." --setting "..." --lighting "..." [--details "..."]`

Generate with the native renderer:
`{{IMAGE_COMMAND}} generate --require-structured --camera "..." --subjects "..." --expression "..." --pose "..." --action "..." --clothing "..." --setting "..." --lighting "..." [--details "..."]`

Execute directly by calling the `terminal` tool function with its per-call argument `timeout=300` seconds for image rendering (not the default 60 seconds). NEVER print the shell command into chat with the human. When the command returns with `send: MEDIA:...`, include that `MEDIA:<path>` line on its own line in your reply. All 8 core parameters must be substantive (at least 2 descriptive words each; placeholders like 'none' are rejected). For longer prompts or requests, use `--request` with a JSON file containing the structured fields and optional `width`, `height`, `seed` and `preset`. The helper automatically adds the entire permanent appearance unchanged; do not shorten or replace it. Other pictured people have their own appearance. Existing eligibility and review preferences apply; use `--intimate` only when eligible. A refusal is not a reason to switch generators. Never guess an output path or claim delivery without a real result. Share the returned `MEDIA:` path only when sending is authorized.

Scheduled photos retain the default recorded-photo prompt and workflow. Do not replace their jobs with this conversation route or rewrite the day for a picture.
